  "offensiveAbilities": [
    {
      "name": "Lesser Mummy Rot",
      "actions": null,
      "traits": [
        "disease",
        "divine",
        "void"
      ],
      "description": "<p>The damage from this disease can't be healed while a creature still has the disease. A creature killed by lesser mummy rot turns to dust and can't be resurrected except by a 7th-rank Resurrect ritual or similar magic</p>\n<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 16 Fortitude save</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> carrier with no ill effect (1 minute)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> <span class=\"roll\" onclick=\"roll(this)\">2d6</span> void damage and Stupefied 1 (1 day)</p>",
      "collapsed": false
    }
  ],
  "spellcastingEntries": [],
  "description": "<p>If a mummy has been in combat, endured the ravages of time, or been exposed to the elements, it can be so damaged it barely functions. These mummies continue guarding their tombs until they are too broken to even move.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The versatility of mummification allows the creation of mummies through a wide range of methods—nature, ritual, alchemy, and combinations of all these.</p>",
  "recallKnowledge": "Religion, DC: 16",
